{
  "_comment": "Per-checkpoint thinking support, keyed by the Hugging Face repo (like data/model-arch.json). mode: 'hybrid' = the serving stack can switch thinking off per request (the `toggle`), so the engine answers interactive traffic in instant mode; 'always' = every answer reasons first (`toggle` is then its effort knob, 'none' when it has none); 'never' = an instruct deployment that answers at once. `default` is the template's mode when the request sets nothing. Evidence: `quote` appears verbatim in `source` (the chat template, the card or the encoding script of the repo); `noThinking` = the template has no thinking block at all. `template` records a hybrid template whose roster entry is served thinking-off. Fetch + verify: `node scripts/thinking-sync.mjs fetch && node scripts/thinking-sync.mjs verify`; `node scripts/arch-sync.mjs build` emits the mode into src/sim/roster.arch.generated.ts.",
